<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil off amid lacklustre demand.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil off amid lacklustre demand.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.6900)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     34.50/34.80     20.41/20.59   34.70/35.00</p>
<p> BREMEN		34.50/34.80     20.41/20.59   34.70/35.00</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    34.50/34.80     20.41/20.59   35.00/35.20</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   35.10/35.20     20.76/20.82   35.60/35.80</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   35.10/35.30     20.76/20 88   35.30/35.50</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  36.30/36.40     21.47/21.53   36.50/36.60</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices weakened on Tuesday in line with falling futures prices and lacklustre demand. Retailers were did some business due more to competitive pricing than strong demand, traders said -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7714.</p>
</text>
